{"id": "sdqa0144", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.55, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1685, "eot_read_ms": 27, "reference_answer": "1955", "query": "When was Rocketdyne founded?", "transcript": "When was Rocketdyne founded?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Once upon a time a small dragon lived in a quiet valley beside a slow green river. Every morning Rocket, the dragon's name, found a shiny rock near the water's edge. One day Rocket found a rock that wasn't shiny at all. It was dull and gray. Rocket was puzzled. Why wasn't this rock like the others? He tried to rub it on his scales, but it didn't change. He asked the wise old turtle by the river, but the turtle just smiled. That evening Rocket sat with the unusual rock in his claws. As he looked at it closely, he noticed tiny marks on its surface, like little stars. Suddenly, the rock began to glow softly. Rocket realized the rock wasn't broken or dull; it was simply different. From that day on, Rocket carried both kinds of rocks—shiny and dull—and learned that being unique is special in its own way.", "answer_ms": 5703}
